te-to-children 22.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a \"Responding to coaching moves\" section to writing-a-passing-plan.md, keyed by move name in field-frequency order, with a one-paragraph technique description and a before/after example for each of the top five moves, plus a one-line index of the remaining registered moves. Cross-link the existing advisory section to it. Content stays in the hand-written guide (the criteria guide is generated; moves are not criteria). Alternative rejected: a generated per-move reference (rebar explain <move>) — larger machinery for content that fits one guide section; revisit if the section outgrows the guide.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md, tests/test_guides.py (text assertions).\n\n## Testing\nText assertions: the section exists; each of the five move names appears with an example block; the [operator-attested] tag appears in the state-attestation-evidence entry; every name matches the coach_moves.py registry spelling.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The guide contains a \"Responding to coaching moves\" section naming the top five moves in frequency order, each with an example (checked: unit test asserting section and move names).\n- [ ] The [operator-attested] AC tag is documented in the guide (checked: text assertion).\n- [ ] Move names match the MOVE_REGISTRY spellings exactly (checked: unit test importing coach_moves).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md","reason":"coaching-moves section"},{"path":"tests/test_guides.py","reason":"text assertions"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","a492-3e46-ca44-40a5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"34c9-8b89-e066-4b09","ticket_type":"task","title":"Add coaching mov